# Patch: BUG-001 — Fix state key inconsistency

## Bug
`get_default_state()` used key `control_flags` but `save_state()`/`load_state()` used `flags`.  
This caused state fields to be inconsistent across code paths.

## Root Cause
`get_default_state()` (line 163) returned `{"control_flags": {...}}`  
`save_state()`/`load_state()` use key `"flags"`

## Fix
Changed line 163 in `scripts/reproctl.py`:
```diff
-        "control_flags": {
+        "flags": {
```

## Verification
```
$ python3 tests/test_state_machine.py
test_state_machine: 3/3 PASS
```

## Rollback
Revert line 163:
```diff
-        "flags": {
+        "control_flags": {
```
